<title>BOSNIA: Bosnia November retail prices up 0.5 mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Bosnia November retail prices up 0.5 mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>SARAJEVO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Statistics Bureau of Bosnia's Moslem-Croat federation issued the following economic indicator details on Monday.</p>
<p>    BOSNIA RETAIL PRICES	  NOV     OCT</p>
<p>    Monthly change (pct)	 +0.5    +1.6</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	  -0.6    -2.3</p>
<p>NOTE -- The data cover 51 percent of Bosnia-Hercegovina territory. Data for remaining 49 percent not available.</p>
<p>Retail prices fell 24.1 percent in Jan-Nov compared with year-ago period. Bosnia's 43-month war ended in December 1996 and a sharp drop in prices followed when goods began flowing into the country at a faster pace.</p>
<p>--Sarajevo newsroom, +387-71-663-864.</p>
